when President Putin ordered the  invasion of Ukraine he provoked Global  outrage but some countries have refused  to condemn the offensive and a few have  even supported it  the result of the vote is  is  March 2022 world leaders voted on a U.N  resolution to demand the end of the war  in Ukraine 141 countries voted in favor  but five voted against the move and 35  abstained  the five countries who voted against the  motion essentially supporting Russia  were Belarus Syria North Korea Eritrea  and Russia itself  Belarus is a major Ally of Putin's in  the region with President Alexander  lukashenko backing him from the start  Russia propped up Syria's Assad regime  in its Civil War and still has forces  there and North Korea and Eritrea are  both ruled by anti-American  dictatorships so were unwilling to  support any pro-western motion Russia's  also historically oppose Western  sanctions in Eritrea  China and Russia say they want to lead a  new world order  but the Ukraine conflict is testing that  relationship China is caught between  supporting an ally and its long-standing  rule that one country should not  interfere in the internal affairs of  another it says Russia's security  concerns are legitimate and refuses to  condemn The Invasion but it also  abstained in that un vote  scrutinizing what happens in Ukraine for  reasons closer to home  [Music]  it wants to seize the island of Taiwan  and sees Ukraine as a test of Western  resolve in a possible precursor to what  might happen in the east Enders  India also abstained in the U.N vote  Russia and India have a close history  prime minister Narendra Modi and Putin  had kept that up  India relies on Russian military  supplies but the war has also put India  in a bind it sees both Russia and the us  as key allies India has tried to stay  neutral about the Ukraine Invasion  calling for sovereignty to be respected  but also for Russia's security concerns  to be addressed but since the U.N vote  there have been signs that India is  becoming more supportive of Ukraine  sending humanitarian Aid and Prime  Minister Modi making a number of calls  to Ukrainian President Vladimir  zielinski  foreign  abstainers in that un vote 17 came from  Africa many have just wanted to stay  neutral but others have openly supported  Russia countries like the Central  African Republic and Mali have close  ties with Russia with Russian  mercenaries helping their respected  governments fighting surgeons  South Africans refused to condemn The  Invasion with President Cyril ramaphosa  criticizing NATO over the conflict  the son of Ugandan president yoweri  musavani even tweeted that the majority  of mankind that are non-whites support  Russia's stand in Ukraine the legacy of  the Cold War is also playing a role  Russia supported other movements that  overthrew western-backed governments in  countries like Algeria Mozambique and  Zimbabwe and its built infrastructure  and provided Aid in military equipment  that soft power approach could now be  paying off  but Putin invaded Ukraine it was widely  thought he sought to undermine NATO and  the West  but ironically it's done the opposite  uniting Europe and forcing even famously  neutral countries like Switzerland to  take a stand  President Putin may have hoped that this  Invasion would Forge A New World Order  he may have won some support from old  allies but the final outcome of this  conflict could be Russia emerging as a  vassal state of China and the West  appearing stronger than many had  expected
 

